 "rationale": "The reference FBR fails on S2 (heavy load) and S4 (weak excitation) due to diode drops and poor impedance matching. A Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) approach uses an inductor to flip the piezo voltage, significantly increasing the energy extracted per cycle. I'm using a half-bridge SSHI with a rectifier to the output to ensure the voltage is clamped and stored efficiently.",
